<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 2.x Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="_Toc235450404" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 12 — Image with an Alt Text</title>
   <refbody>
      <section id="sec_d365e7">
         <p>The alt attribute on an HTML <codeph>&lt;img&gt;</codeph> element provides a short text description of the image for readers who cannot see it, such as those using screen readers. It is a required attribute for accessibility compliance.</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Image with alt text</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>HTML Input</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock id="codeblock_g12_rd4_lkc">
&lt;img src="media/print_head_diagram.png"
     alt="Diagram showing the print head path inside the printer"/></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                    
                   
                    
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock id="codeblock_yr5_td4_lkc">
&lt;image href="media/print_head_diagram.png">
  &lt;alt>Diagram showing the print head path inside the printer&lt;/alt>
&lt;/image></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
         <p>
            <b>Result:</b> The converter extracts the <codeph>alt</codeph> attribute value from the HTML <codeph>&lt;img&gt;</codeph> element and maps it to the DITA <codeph>&lt;alt&gt;</codeph> element inside <codeph>&lt;image&gt;</codeph>, preserving the image description for accessibility and assistive technologies.</p>
      </section>
   </refbody>
</reference>
